ets#Workflow update set migration use case - subflow dependency \\(risk\\)#{10}":[104,105],"#Workflow movement with update sets#Workflow update set migration use case - subflow dependency \\(risk\\)#{11}":[106,107],"#Workflow movement with update sets#Workflow update set migration use case - subflow dependency \\(risk\\)#{12}":[108,108],"#Workflow movement with update sets#Workflow update set migration use case - subflow dependency \\(risk\\)#{13}":[109,109],"#Workflow movement with update sets#Workflow update set migration use case - subflow dependency \\(risk\\)#{14}":[110,111],"#Workflow movement with update sets#Workflow update set migration use case - subflow dependency \\(risk\\)#{15}":[112,113],"#Workflow movement with update sets#Workflow update set migration use case - subflow dependency \\(risk\\)#{16}":[114,114],"#Workflow movement with update sets#Workflow update set migration use case - subflow dependency \\(risk\\)#{17}":[115,115],"#Workflow movement with update sets#Workflow update set migration use case - subflow dependency \\(risk\\)#{18}":[116,117],"#Workflow movement with update sets#Workflow update set migration use case - subflow dependency \\(risk\\)#{19}":[118,119],"#Workflow movement with update sets#Workflow update set migration use case - subflow dependency \\(risk\\)#{20}":[120,121],"#Workflow movement with update sets#Workflow update set migration use case - subflow dependency \\(risk\\)#{21}":[122,123],"#Workflow movement with update sets#Workflow update set migration use case - subflow dependency \\(risk\\)#{22}":[124,124],"#Workflow movement with update sets#Workflow update set migration use case - subflow dependency \\(risk\\)#{23}":[125,125],"#Workflow movement with update sets#Workflow update set migration use case - subflow dependency \\(risk\\)#{24}":[126,128]},"outlinks":[{"title":"workflow is published","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/servicenow-platform/legacy-workflow/work-on-workflows.md","line":25},{"title":"System update sets","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/application-development/system-update-sets.md","line":27},{"title":"Workflow administration","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/servicenow-platform/legacy-workflow/c_WorkflowAdministration.md","line":29},{"title":"ValidateUpdateSetDependencies","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/servicenow-platform/legacy-workflow/r_VldtUpdtStDpnd.md","line":85},{"title":"validates","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/servicenow-platform/legacy-workflow/c_WorkflowValidation.md","line":108},{"title":"ValidateUpdateSetDependencies","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/servicenow-platform/legacy-workflow/r_VldtUpdtStDpnd.md","line":118}],"metadata":{"title":"Workflow movement with update sets","description":"The system tracks workflows in update sets differently than other records because workflow information is stored across multiple tables.Create a new workflow with no dependencies and then migrate the workflow in an update set.Successfully edit and migrate an existing workflow and its dependent subflow.Edit and migrate an existing workflow from a test instance to a production instance that fails to run on the production instance because of a missing dependent subflow.Multiple users migrate a workflow from a test instance to a production instance without proper coordination. This use case can succeed, but only when each user understands the dependencies and properly migrates the dependent parts of the workflow to the new instance.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/legacy-workflow/c\\_WorkflowMovementWithUpdateSets.html","release":"australia","product":"Legacy Workflow","cla